      "response": {
        "content": "The proposed AppSpec for **flyway-flyway** is finalized and pending your confirmation.\n\n**What it does:** Combines bird GPS tags and surface wind over your bbox (50 m cells) into an authority-only score heat-map. Tags drive a `dwell` operator (places birds land and linger) weighted 0.8 and a `flow_source` operator (fast, fairly straight flight between stops) weighted 0.7. Wind drives a `field` operator weighted 0.5 using `wind_speed_10m` / `wind_direction_10m` as a vector field with direction convention \"from\".\n\n**Tiering & visibility:** `tags` is flexible (crowd-sourced bird reporters/devices), authority visibility. `wind` is stiff (official weather feed), authority visibility. No locked inputs, so verification starts with `predictive_check` at priority 1.\n\n**Plausibility (tags):** max_speed_mps 20, jitter_m 10, flag_constant_speed true (birds don't normally fly at one unchanging speed), flag_straight_line false (meaning says flights are fairly straight, so real tracks won't be wrongly flagged).\n\n**Outputs:** `score` layer authority visibility; POI labels mode `on` with label_set `water`, `roost`, `feeding ground` (none sensitive, none destinations since the intent names places but doesn't direct users to them). Routing disabled — no destination is requested.\n\n**Connector:** `wind` pull input keeps its `json_api` / `open_meteo` connector (poll 900 s, lat/lon as given).\n\nConfirm when you're ready to activate."
